.TH EDITLINE 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
editline \- command-line editing and history interface
.SH LIBRARY
Editline library (libedit, \-ledit)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <histedit.h>
.PP
.B typedef struct editline EditLine;
.br
.B typedef struct history History;
.br
.B typedef const char *(*el_pfunc_t)(EditLine *);
.br
.B typedef unsigned char (*el_func_t)(EditLine *, int);
.PP
.B typedef struct lineinfo {
.br
.BI "    const char *buffer;"
.br
.BI "    const char *cursor;"
.br
.BI "    const char *lastchar;"
.br
.B } LineInfo;
.PP
.B typedef struct hist_event {
.br
.BI "    int num;"
.br
.BI "    const char *str;"
.br
.B } HistEvent;
.PP
.BI "EditLine *el_init(const char *prog, FILE *fin, FILE *fout, FILE *ferr);"
.br
.BI "void el_end(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "void el_reset(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "const char *el_gets(EditLine *el, int *count);"
.br
.BI "int el_set(EditLine *el, int op, ...);"
.br
.BI "int el_get(EditLine *el, int op, ...);"
.br
.BI "void el_resize(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "int el_source(EditLine *el, const char *file);"
.br
.BI "const LineInfo *el_line(EditLine *el);"
.br
.BI "int el_insertstr(EditLine *el, const char *str);"
.br
.BI "void el_deletestr(EditLine *el, int count);"
.br
.BI "int el_replacestr(EditLine *el, const char *str);"
.PP
.BI "History *history_init(void);"
.br
.BI "void history_end(History *h);"
.br
.BI "int history(History *h, HistEvent *ev, int op, ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B editline
library provides interactive line editing, key binding, prompt handling,
and command history support for user-space programs.
.PP
Public interfaces are grouped as:
.TP
.B Session lifecycle
.BR el_init (3),
.BR el_end (3),
.BR el_reset (3)
.TP
.B Interactive input
.BR el_gets (3),
.BR el_line (3),
.BR el_insertstr (3),
.BR el_deletestr (3)
.TP
.B Configuration
.BR el_set (3),
.BR el_get (3),
.BR el_source (3)
.TP
.B History
.BR history (3),
.BR history_init (3),
.BR history_end (3)
.TP
.B Tokenizer
.BR tok_init (3),
.BR tok_end (3),
.BR tok_reset (3),
.BR tok_str (3)
.SH EDITING MODES
.SS Emacs Mode (default)
Emacs-style editing is the default mode.
Standard bindings include:
.TP
.B ^A / ^E
Beginning / end of line.
.TP
.B ^B / ^F
Move backward / forward one character.
.TP
.B M-b / M-f
Move backward / forward one word.
.TP
.B ^D
Delete character at cursor (or indicate EOF on empty line).
.TP
.B ^K
Kill from cursor to end of line.
.TP
.B ^U
Unix line discard (kill from beginning to cursor).
.TP
.B ^W
Unix word rubout.
.TP
.B ^Y
Yank (paste) killed text.
.TP
.B ^_
Undo last edit.
.TP
.B ^T
Transpose characters.
.TP
.B TAB
Filename completion.
.SS Vi Mode
Vi mode is activated by calling:
.RS
.nf
el_set(el, EL_EDITOR, "vi");
.fi
.RE
.PP
Vi mode provides two sub-modes:
.TP
.B Insert Mode
Characters are inserted at the cursor.
Press
.B ESC
to enter command mode.
Insert mode is the default when vi mode is first selected.
.TP
.B Command Mode
Single-key commands move the cursor and manipulate text.
Press
.B i
to return to insert mode.
.PP
Command-mode key bindings include:
.TP
.B h / l
Move left / right one character.
.TP
.B w / b / e
Move forward / backward by word, or to end of word.
.TP
.B 0 / $
Move to beginning / end of line.
.TP
.B x / X
Delete character at / before cursor.
.TP
.B d
Delete (followed by a motion).
.TP
.B c
Change (delete then enter insert mode).
.TP
.B y
Yank (copy, followed by a motion).
.TP
.B p / P
Put yanked text after / before cursor.
.TP
.B r
Replace one character.
.TP
.B .
Repeat last change.
.TP
.B u
Undo.
.TP
.B /\fIpattern\fR
Search history forward for
.IR pattern .
.TP
.B ?\fIpattern\fR
Search history backward for
.IR pattern .
.TP
.B n / N
Repeat last search in same / opposite direction.
.TP
.B f\fIc\fR / F\fIc\fR
Find character
.I c
forward / backward on current line.
.TP
.B ;\fR / \fB,
Repeat / reverse last find character command.
.SH COMPLETION
The completion callback is registered via:
.RS
.nf
el_set(el, EL_ADDFN, "complete", "Complete filename",
       my_complete_func);
el_set(el, EL_BIND, "^I", "complete", NULL);
.fi
.RE
.PP
A completion function has the signature:
.RS
.nf
unsigned char my_complete(EditLine *el, int ch);
.fi
.RE
.PP
When invoked, the function should inspect the current line via
.BR el_line (3),
determine possible completions, and insert the result using
.BR el_insertstr (3).
Return
.B CC_NORM
to redraw the line, or
.B CC_ERROR
on failure.
.SH PUBLIC MACROS
Public operation macros used with
.BR el_set ()
and
.BR el_get ()
include:
.TP
.B EL_PROMPT
Set/get the primary prompt callback.  The
.BR el_set ()
argument is an
.I el_pfunc_t
and
.BR el_get ()
stores an
.I el_pfunc_t
in the caller-supplied pointer.
.TP
.B EL_PROMPT_ESC
Set/get the primary prompt callback plus the character used to mark
non-printing prompt escape spans.
.TP
.B EL_RPROMPT
Set/get the right-side prompt callback.
.TP
.B EL_RPROMPT_ESC
Set/get the right-side prompt callback plus the non-printing escape marker.
.TP
.B EL_EDITOR
Set/get editing mode (for example, "emacs" or "vi").
.TP
.B EL_SIGNAL
Enable or disable internal signal handling.
.TP
.B EL_BIND
Configure key bindings.
.TP
.B EL_ADDFN
Register a custom editor function.
.TP
.B EL_HIST
Attach a history backend callback and handle.
.TP
.B EL_GETCFN
Set/get low-level character input callback.
.TP
.B EL_CLIENTDATA
Set/get application-owned opaque pointer.
.TP
.B EL_REFRESH
Request immediate redisplay.
.TP
.B EL_GETTC
Query terminal capability values.
.TP
.B EL_SETTY
Apply tty mode presets.
.TP
.B EL_GETFP
Fetch the input, output, or error stream.
.TP
.B EL_SETFP
Set the input, output, or error stream.
.PP
Public history operation macros used with
.BR history ()
include:
.TP
.B H_ENTER
Append a new entry.
.TP
.B H_APPEND
Append text to current entry.
.TP
.B H_PREV
Move to previous entry.
.TP
.B H_NEXT
Move to next entry.
.TP
.B H_CURR
Read current entry.
.TP
.B H_FIRST
Move to oldest entry.
.TP
.B H_LAST
Move to newest entry.
.TP
.B H_SET
Jump to entry by index.
.TP
.B H_CLEAR
Remove all entries.
.TP
.B H_LOAD
Load history from file.
.TP
.B H_SAVE
Save history to file.
.TP
.B H_SETSIZE
Set history size limit.
.TP
.B H_GETSIZE
Get history size limit.
.TP
.B H_SETUNIQUE
Enable or disable duplicate suppression.
.TP
.B H_GETUNIQUE
Get duplicate suppression state.
.TP
.B H_END
End history traversal state.
.PP
Public editor command return macros are:
.BR CC_NORM ,
.BR CC_NEWLINE ,
.BR CC_EOF ,
and
.BR CC_ERROR .
.SH THREAD SAFETY
An
.B EditLine
handle is not thread-safe.
Applications must confine each handle to one thread at a time and
serialize external access.
.SH EXAMPLES
The following program reads and echoes one edited line:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
#include <histedit.h>
#include <stdio.h>

static const char *
prompt(EditLine *el)
{
    (void)el;
    return "> ";
}

int
main(void)
{
    EditLine *el = el_init("prog", stdin, stdout, stderr);
    int count;
    const char *line;

    el_set(el, EL_PROMPT, prompt);
    line = el_gets(el, &count);
    if (line != NULL && count > 0)
        printf("read: %s", line);
    el_end(el);
    return 0;
}
.EE
.RE
